Z||000000||ordovician||12-18-2001||06:14 PM||||when i pull my e-brake up, it falls back down. to disengage it, i pull it up, push the button, and let the tension off.<BR>because it falls down, i forget its on sometimes, and screw up my brakes in the process. is it supposed to do this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ejayerik||12-18-2001||06:17 PM||||I have the same problem. My clicking thing on the parking brake is broken. I just curb the car because I live on a hill. If I put it into gear to park it, it just shimms downhill. It will go, stop, go, stop. Very strange. I am in the proccess of ordering a new parking brake mechanism. I'll let you know if it fixes the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||12-18-2001||06:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ordovician:<BR><B>when i pull my e-brake up, it falls back down. to disengage it, i pull it up, push the button, and let the tension off... is it supposed to do this?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Yes, it's supposed to go back down.  Otherwise, it'd be right there in the way, after you set the brake and tried to exit the car.<P>The "dingy box" should chime, and warning light on dash should help you remember to release the E-brake before driving off. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-18-2001||06:26 PM||||I think they're supposed to be that way..<BR>Every Fiero I've seen, including mine, does it. <P>Otherwise, how would you get out?<P>The brake light on dash should come on, mine dings when it is on also.<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">        <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed </FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
